  'website.publish_prompt_body': [
    '请使用 Sites 插件，帮我上传并部署 Lumi 生成的静态网站。\n{source}\n\n1. 先读取目录内的 README.md，确认 index.html、rss.xml、static/、data/、media/ 齐全。若无法访问该目录，请让我提供文件夹；若缺少生成文件，请提示我回 Lumi 更新网站。\n2. 将网站复制到独立的发布工作目录，所有修改只作用于副本，保留 Lumi 管理的原 website/。保留现有绘本翻页／条漫阅读、手机适配和图片懒加载。\n3. 按 Sites 的静态站点流程打包并部署网站，以 index.html 为入口，保留 static/、data/、media/ 和 rss.xml 的相对目录结构。只发布这些网站文件，不上传项目数据库、原始 assets/、聊天记录或其他无关文件。\n4. 必须替换 RSS：用 Sites 实际返回的网站完整目录地址（包含协议和部署子路径，末尾不加 /），替换副本 rss.xml 中所有 {token}。正确处理 URL 编码及 XML／HTML 转义，保留章节 GUID 和日期。如果首次部署后才能取得地址，替换后再次部署；最终发布版本不能残留占位符。\n5. 检查线上首页、章节导航、绘本／条漫阅读和图片加载，并检查 rss.xml 可解析、章节链接与图片地址指向最终网站。完成后给我网站链接、RSS 订阅链接和当前访问范围；如访问权限限制了 RSS 订阅，请明确说明。\n\n执行效率要求：\n- 按现有静态网站直接部署，不重新设计、不引入框架或依赖。\n- 精准发现所需工具，只读取当前步骤需要的工具说明，避免输出完整工具目录。\n- 优先通过脚本检查文件、路径、RSS 和资源完整性，只返回摘要、数量和异常；避免打印完整源码、全部文件列表或完整 DOM。\n- 合并独立检查，减少工具往返。已经通过且输入未改变的检查不再重复。\n- 浏览器只验证代表性流程：首页、章节切换、手机布局和滚动懒加载；所有资源是否可访问交给脚本批量检查。\n- 出错时只针对具体原因诊断和修复，不扩展为全面排查。\n- 保持默认访问权限。若登录阻碍浏览器验证，优先使用 Sites 支持的授权访问；仍无法验证时明确报告限制，不自行搭建额外代理。\n- 最后只报告网站链接、RSS 链接、访问范围、验证结果和必要限制。\n\n这些要求用于减少无效工作，不得省略原任务要求的文件保护、RSS 替换、上传范围检查或部署结果核验。',
    'Use the Sites plugin to upload and deploy my static website generated by Lumi.\n{source}\n\n1. Read README.md and confirm index.html, rss.xml, static/, data/, and media/ are present. If the directory is inaccessible, ask me to provide it. If generated files are missing, ask me to update the website in Lumi.\n2. Copy the website into a separate publishing workspace and make all changes there, preserving the original Lumi-managed website/ directory. Keep the existing picture-book / vertical-comic reader, mobile layout, and image lazy loading.\n3. Package and deploy using the Sites static-site workflow, with index.html as the entry point and the relative structure of static/, data/, media/, and rss.xml intact. Publish only these website files, excluding project databases, original assets/, chat logs, and unrelated files.\n4. Replace the RSS token: use the actual full website directory URL returned by Sites, including the scheme and deployment subpath with no trailing slash, to replace every {token} in the copied rss.xml. Handle URL encoding and XML/HTML escaping correctly, preserving chapter GUIDs and dates. If the URL is only available after an initial deployment, replace the token and deploy again. The final deployed feed must contain no placeholders.\n5. Verify the deployed homepage, chapter navigation, picture-book / comic reader, images, and parseable rss.xml whose chapter and image links point to the final website. Return the website URL, RSS subscription URL, and current audience. Explain any access restrictions that prevent RSS subscriptions.\n\nExecution efficiency requirements:\n- Deploy the existing static website directly without redesigning it or introducing frameworks or dependencies.\n- Discover tools precisely and read only the tool documentation needed for the current step. Avoid printing the full tool catalog.\n- Prefer scripts to check files, paths, RSS, and resource integrity. Return only summaries, counts, and exceptions; avoid printing entire source files, complete file lists, or full DOM snapshots.\n- Batch independent checks to reduce tool round trips. Do not repeat successful checks when their inputs have not changed.\n- Use the browser only for representative flows: the homepage, chapter switching, mobile layout, and scrolling lazy loading. Check accessibility of all resources in a batch script.\n- Diagnose and fix only the specific cause of an error instead of expanding into a broad investigation.\n- Keep the default access permissions. If login blocks browser verification, prefer authorized access supported by Sites. If verification remains unavailable, clearly report the limitation without creating an additional proxy.\n- In the final response, report only the website URL, RSS URL, audience, verification results, and necessary limitations.\n\nThese requirements reduce unnecessary work and must not omit the original task requirements for protecting source files, replacing RSS placeholders, checking upload scope, or verifying the deployment result.',
  ],
